@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Copyright Policy & Content Creator Rights — SaveZonix";
}

<section class="legal-page">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
        <partial name="_LegalNav" model='(string)"Copyright"' />

        <div class="legal-header">
            <h1 class="legal-title">Copyright Policy &amp; Creator Rights Protection</h1>
            <div class="legal-meta">
                <span>International Copyright Treaties &bull; WIPO &bull; Berne Convention</span>
                <span>Last Updated: October 19, 2026</span>
                <span>Creator Rights &bull; Anti-Piracy Framework</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-content">
            <div class="highlight-box">
                <strong>Our Commitment to Intellectual Property:</strong> SaveZonix respects the rights of artists, digital creators, musicians, filmmakers, and broadcasters worldwide. Our software is designed strictly as a neutral client-side protocol analysis utility. We categorically oppose commercial digital piracy and enforce strict safeguards to ensure our tools are not used to infringe exclusive intellectual property rights.
            </div>

            <h2>1. Neutral Dual-Use Protocol Architecture</h2>
            <p>SaveZonix operates as a client-side media transport inspector, analogous to web browsers, developer network debuggers, and open tools like <code>curl</code> and <code>ffmpeg</code>. The software does not maintain any searchable catalog, index, library, torrent tracker, or repository of copyrighted multimedia works.</p>

            <h2>2. User Responsibility &amp; Statutory Authorization</h2>
            <p>All download operations are initiated solely, directly, and unilaterally by individual users on their personal devices. Users bear the sole and exclusive legal responsibility for ensuring they possess the necessary rights, licenses, or statutory exemptions to record or archive any media accessed.</p>

            <h2>3. Anti-Infringement &amp; Anti-DRM Safeguards</h2>
            <p>SaveZonix incorporates the following affirmative architectural safeguards to protect intellectual property:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>No Commercial DRM Circumvention:</strong> The software contains no decryption keys, algorithmic bypasses, or reverse-engineering mechanisms for hardware or software Digital Rights Management (DRM) technologies (including Widevine, FairPlay, PlayReady, or HDCP). DRM-protected commercial streams cannot be decrypted.</li>
                <li><strong>No Centralized Media Cache:</strong> No media content is stored, cached, indexed, or hosted on SaveZonix servers. Media packets travel directly between the origin CDN and the user's personal computer.</li>
                <li><strong>No Content Promotion:</strong> SaveZonix does not promote, link to, or suggest unauthorized downloads of commercial Hollywood films, subscription television, or copyrighted musical albums.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. Third-Party Trademarks &amp; Brand Rights</h2>
            <p>All product names, logos, brands, and registered trademarks mentioned on this website (such as YouTube, Vimeo, Twitch, TikTok, Instagram, Meta, PixelFlix, and others) belong exclusively to their respective owners. Mention of these platforms is made purely for technical compatibility reference under the doctrine of nominative fair use and does not imply endorsement, sponsorship, or affiliation.</p>

            <h2>5. Assistance for Rights Holders</h2>
            <p>If you are a copyright owner or intellectual property counsel with inquiries or concerns regarding SaveZonix, please refer to our <a asp-controller="Legal" asp-action="DMCA" class="auth-link">DMCA Procedure</a> or reach our legal department at <a href="mailto:savezonix@gmail.com" class="auth-link">savezonix@gmail.com</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
